{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "06bd4650-f075-43c4-8bb4-75dec4bfc573",
    "name": "Quizly",
    "description": "Full happy-path / unhappy-path test suite for the Quizly backend.\n\nIMPORTANT: Run the whole collection top-to-bottom (Collection Runner), not individual requests in isolation. Later requests depend on environment variables (usernames, quizId) set by earlier ones.\n\nAuthentication works with HttpOnly cookies. Postman stores the cookies from the login response automatically and sends them with every following request, so no Authorization header is needed. To switch users the collection simply logs in as the other user; logout removes the cookies again.\n\n'happy path > Quizzes > create_quiz' really downloads the YouTube video, transcribes it with Whisper and asks Gemini. This can take a minute; use a short video in the environment variable 'youtube_url'.\n\nThe 'cleanup' folder must run last: it deletes the quiz and checks that the old refresh token is blacklisted after logout.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
